  "text": "How do rich people turn one property into five? Mr. Bean buys a single apartment for $200 ,000. He puts down 20%. That's $40 ,000. The bank lends him the rest. He rents it out for $2 ,000 a month. The tenant pays the mortgage. Now, Mr. Bean owns an asset that makes money while he sleeps. But he doesn't stop there. He takes the equity from the first property and uses it as a down payment on a second one. The bank sees the first property is performing well. They approve the second loan easily now he owns two properties both are paying down their mortgages he repeats the process again three four five properties each one is a money -making machine the tenants pay the debt the properties go up in value mr bean builds wealth without using his own cash this is called the brr strategy buy renovate rent refinance repeat but here's the secret most people get stuck at one property because they wait to save cash the rich don't wait they use the bank's money money, and the property's value, they turn one house into a portfolio. If you want to learn how to do this, follow for more real estate secrets.",
